  "limitations": [
    "One fresh normally trusted observation per phase, through exact document completion including FIN. First accepted is not first sent; duplicates, loss and packetization can make a sample ineligible for this comparison.",
    "The one-byte frame-type width is derived from the immutable nginx minimal serializer, not measured by the frozen dispatched-frame observer. Other header widths are observed.",
    "Each phase retains its actual response stream data size. Date and other HTTP/3 headers may vary while the complete encoded body remains exactly 389 B; total stream payloads are not asserted byte-identical.",
    "The 5 B difference concerns the selected response STREAM headers only. It is not a fixed encrypted, packet, whole-exchange, HTTP/2, timing or peer saving.",
    "Image/page/TLS pointers are checked before and after. Coarse host readback clocks and command order are not a per-request worker-generation attestation."
  ]
